rison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:16:### B. Hold the company's core figures (mechanism 1): needs Alex to lift D505\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:22:### C. Open more of the rule-allowed big matters (framing and coverage)\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:33:## The arithmetic\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:37:## The order and the cost\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:39:2. **B** probe on stored states: cents, but only if Alex lifts D505.\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:44:## Census C ($0), 2026-11-19: why the 14 rule-allowed matters are lost\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md:59:## Check A ($0), 2026-11-19: what the 46 no-ladder theses bundle\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:1:# Design: a thesis the ladder refuses is not open (fix 1 of PATH-TO-PASS; $0 design, nothing built)\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:14:  - The evidence the answer linked only to it is kept unlinked (D383), so the later-linking step can file it.\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:18:## State × event\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:30:## Value × reader\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:35:- **Evidence linked only to a refused thesis:** unlinked, read by Step 2 and by later linking (D383, D513).\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:37:## New path × old checks\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:43:## Prior decisions\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:46:| D383 | A kept statement no thesis takes is kept and linked later | Holds |\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:53:**Not decided here:** the ladder's own refusal of a deal's completion and size (fix 3), and D505 (fix 4).\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:58:## Blind review, round 1 (`council-e-codex.md`): NOT READY. Gaps to close in the next revision\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:73:## Revision 2: the four gaps closed\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:93:  - an evidence item left with no link moves to `unfiled_evidence`, the runner's existing field (D383).\ndocs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/DESIGN-refused-not-open.md:115:## Blind review, round 2 (`council-f-codex.md`): NOT READY. Remaining gaps\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1:# Hivemind architecture: a market world model built the way a hedge-fund analyst works\nclean-arch/PRD.md:14:## 1. Vision, problems and what is done differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:16:### 1.1 The vision: a market world model\nclean-arch/PRD.md:55:### 1.2 The problems it answers\nclean-arch/PRD.md:79:### 1.3 Why the running pipeline was rebuilt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:102:### 1.4 What the new system does differently\nclean-arch/PRD.md:107:| What opens a question | Extraction proposes candidates with answer choices; a matcher and a collision judge decide. | Step 1 decides in the same reading, and only for a big matter; a company's own figures are conditions, not questions (D382, D384). | 1 of 10 opened wrongly on 50 fresh articles (D386). Opening is also where it loses most against the ruler (section 8). |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:108:| A useful fact no question takes | Thrown away. | Kept without links, and offered to each new question when it opens (D383). | 0 thrown away against 278 in one fresh week; but 389 of 569 kept statements were read by no judgement that week (section 10). |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:126:### 1.5 What decides that it replaces the running pipeline (D665, superseding D548's gate order)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:171:## 2. Architecture at a glance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:222:## 3. The information the system works with\nclean-arch/PRD.md:239:## 4. Step 1: read the item\nclean-arch/PRD.md:241:### Input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:248:### What the model decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:259:   covers it opens (D383; Alex: \"先存着，有观点再挂\").\nclean-arch/PRD.md:263:- **A financial figure is a condition, not a thesis** (D382; Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\").\nclean-arch/PRD.md:265:  evidence for the judgements of related questions (D505).\nclean-arch/PRD.md:273:### Output\nclean-arch/PRD.md:282:### Example\nclean-arch/PRD.md:294:## 5. Step 2: find and compare related evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:296:### Why this is separate\nclean-arch/PRD.md:300:### Find candidate evidence\nclean-arch/PRD.md:308:### Compare with Jev\nclean-arch/PRD.md:349:## 6. Step 3: save evidence and links\nclean-arch/PRD.md:358:| Material statement no thesis takes | The evidence, kept in the company's record without links (D383). When a thesis opens, Jev is asked of each earlier unlinked group whether it informs the thesis; a yes adds the link (section 13). |\nclean-arch/PRD.md:363:## 7. Step 4: judge the thesis\nclean-arch/PRD.md:370:### Two parts\nclean-arch/PRD.md:379:### What the ladder step decides\nclean-arch/PRD.md:396:### Where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:409:## 8. How the system is measured, and where it stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:411:### The measuring stick\nclean-arch/PRD.md:423:### Where each step stands\nclean-arch/PRD.md:434:### What the measurements say\nclean-arch/PRD.md:450:## 9. Walk one item through the system\nclean-arch/PRD.md:472:## 10. Open questions\nclean-arch/PRD.md:483:   company's kept figures reach the judgements of related questions (D505); the delivery gap is an open defect.\nclean-arch/PRD.md:495:## 11. Design boundary\nclean-arch/PRD.md:503:## 12. Step 1 prompt: c8, adopted (D387)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:517:  code checks each value against a verified passage (D382).\nclean-arch/PRD.md:520:- **A material statement that no thesis takes is kept without links**, and is linked later when a covering thesis opens (D383). What\nclean-arch/PRD.md:533:### What the model receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:539:### System prompt\nclean-arch/PRD.md:717:### Closing check\nclean-arch/PRD.md:740:### Proposed per-item input\nclean-arch/PRD.md:767:### Structured-output schema\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1058:### Illustrative output for the sample input (earlier Luna draft, kept as history)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1127:### Mapping to the Step 1 diagram\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1139:### Request review and remaining limits\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1147:## 13. Step 2 prompt: Jev request (frozen)\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1151:### What Jev receives\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1159:### The question\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1172:### How the answers become the outcome\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1179:### The later link when a thesis opens\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1191:## 14. Existing components to reference during the rebuild\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1195:### Thesis and evidence database\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1203:### Source pool and golden validation data\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1214:### Source data standing in for Hummingbird\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1222:### Existing extraction reference split\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1235:### Diagram-to-code map\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1250:## 15. Future design: entity relationships and cross-entity linkage\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1254:### Why this is needed\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1258:### Separate, asynchronous relationship maintenance\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1268:### Illustration: a supplier disruption\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1272:### Questions to resolve before cross-entity production use\nclean-arch/PRD.md:1284:## 16. Earlier record\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1:# Decisions\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:23:## Open for Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:## Settled in this consolidation\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:49:## 1. System (PRD 00)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:75:## Latest decision: remove the separate earnings-report import (D370)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:79:## Latest decision: current and future financial evidence (D371)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:83:## Latest decision: continue scoring on the existing gold (D373)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:87:## Latest decision: read the current library for each item (D375)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:91:## Latest decision: return complete evidence without the 1 MB rejection (D376)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:95:## Latest decision: return the full question catalog without the 150 KB rejection (D377)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:99:## 2. Research universe (PRD 01)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:110:## 3. Classification (PRD 02)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:120:## 4. Config (PRD 03)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:129:## 5. Dispatch (PRD 04)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:137:## 6. Extraction (PRD 05 and the extraction standard)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:172:## 7. Thesis library (PRD 06)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:239:## 8. Closing and pull mode (PRD 07, PRD 08)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:251:## 9. Review pool (PRD 09)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:257:## 10. Current phase: filing that links facts the way an analyst does (PRD 10)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:294:## 12. Idea API and service (docs/poc/idea-card.md, docs/poc/service.md)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:312:## 13. Data (README, \"Local requirements and data\")\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:320:## 14. Operations (README, AGENTS §9)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:332:## 15. Working rules (AGENTS.md)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:340:## Index\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:553:| D209 | 2026-10-28 | A statement no open question takes is dropped at extraction; evaluation reads the dropped record, not a sid… | in force (amended by D264; for the clean path by D382, D383) | §6 Extraction |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:726:| D382 | 2026-11-08 | Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason | in force | clean-arch PRD §12 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:727:| D383 | 2026-11-08 | D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later | in force; amends D209 | clean-arch PRD §§5, 12 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:833:| D489 | 2026-11-14 | The fresh week (one draw a system): not clear by the rule written before reading, no system chosen; production covers 4 of 5 big matters and the clean path 2 (it lacks revenue and margin, D382/D384); whether the new system holds questions on the company's main numbers goes to Alex with three options (council consensus) | in force; Alex chose the test (D490) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/WEEK-RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:834:| D490 | 2026-11-14 | Alex opens a test arm of clean Step 1 that may open questions on the company's revenue and margin (\"试开这类问题\"): a probe of a few cents on the stored week first, the second fresh week only if it meets its lines; D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path | in force; the test ran and its arm was stopped (D491) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:849:| D505 | 2026-11-15 | Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions (not a table, not questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand); first a $0 check on the stored fresh-week run: is a kept financial figure a judgement should have received absent from its request | in force; the check ran (D506) | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` §11 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:908:| D564 | 2026-11-16 | The fortnight read (council consensus): no held question re-opened; gate 1 still not met in the product condition (7 or 5 of 13 right); no last answer unsupported by both readers, 6 of 12 contested; the page fix (processing steps and completed days at the writer) accepted for completed replays; the due-date class is one matter; next a $0 sizing of D505's company-figure delivery gap, facts linked elsewhere included | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-run/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:953:| D609 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council, cold Codex read): the next production step is a $0 source-to-request trace of the company's own figures on the carried fortnight (D505), by member, with time, duplicate, population and relevance controls and an independent second reader on bearing cases; moves only on a shared, consequential delivery mechanism | in force | `reflection-5/codex-cold.md`, `reflection-5/codex-challenge-1.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:954:| D610 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council): the company-figure delivery route closes narrowly (5 bearing undelivered statements on 3 questions, two mechanisms, none predicted to move an answer by a blind second reader with working controls; 49 groups homeless by D382/D384); no v12 effect test; next a $0 feasibility review of a same-news product comparison from established libraries | in force | `delivery-trace/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1020:| D676 | 2026-11-19 | Release comparison (5-draw diagnostic): new loses (2–3 vs 10 of 32) for two known mechanisms, D382's figure exclusion and the Step 1→ladder bundled-question loss (D432); measurement sound; even repaired the new system ties at best; keep the old system; attainable verdict computed before any future paid comparison (council consensus) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1021:| D677 | 2026-11-19 | The release comparison's goal loop closed: the old system stays, no paid work continues; reversed only if Alex reverses D505 or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first (council consensus, D439/D544) | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-c-codex.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
