{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'p=poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\ncat \"$p\"/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/mapping.json\ncat \"$p\"/reading-diagnostic/eligibility.json | head -85\ncat \"$p\"/run/ledgers/{old-1,old-2,old-3,new-2,new-3}.json\nhead -2 \"$p\"/run/ledgers/new-2.attempts.jsonl\nhead -1 \"$p\"/run/new-2/judge/spend.jsonl\nhead -1 \"$p\"/run/new-2/ladder/spend.jsonl\ncat \"$p\"/run/new-2/judge/draw-new-2/adapter-counts.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/claude-reflection.md\nsed -n '344,370p' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md\nls clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13 | rg 'comparison|budget|diagnost|release|measure|slice|count'\nrg -n '\"'^PRICES|CACHED_INPUT_SHARE|gpt-6-(astra|luna)'\"' hivemind/model.py\nrg -n '\"'^def '\"' clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/ladder_adapter.py | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/claude-reflection.md\nsed -n '344,370p' docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md\nls clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13 | rg 'comparison|budget|diagnost|release|measure|slice|count'\nrg -n '\"'^PRICES|CACHED_INPUT_SHARE|gpt-6-(astra|luna)'\"' hivemind/model.py\nrg -n '\"'^def '\"' clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/ladder_adapter.py | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"# Claude's reflection, written before reading Codex's independent review\n\n## Did we measure wrong?\nNo. The reading measured what it was built to measure, which is the products as configured (D667).\n- **The matter list is independent of both systems.** It was built by blind readers from the 410 kept articles; neither system's\n  output went into it.\n- **The mapping was done blind**, by two reader families plus third readers.\n- **All controls pass:** 6 of 6 plants, 4 of 4 supported controls, 3 of 3 repeats.\n- **The old system's served cards hold up** on four I read against their material: FY27 data-center revenue, FY28 revenue, FY27 gross\n  margin and hyperscaler capex. Both readers did the arithmetic.\n- **No new-system question was wrongly mapped out.** Its libraries at the cutoff contain no question on the 7–8 old-only matters.\n\n## Why the new system loses: two mechanisms, both known before the run\n\n**1. By design, D382, D384 and D505: the company's own figures are not questions.**\n- 7 of the 32 matters are company figures, and the old system serves 5–6 of them.\n- D667 itself says: \"The new system does not open such questions by D505, and Alex sees how much of any gap that makes.\"\n- The week of 2026-09-22 to 09-28 (D489) had already shown the same thing: production 4 of 5 big matters, clean 2, for this cause.\n\n**2. A broken hand-off between Step 1 and the ladder.**\n- Step 1 opens compound questions: two years in one question, or several figures or outcomes in one. The frozen ladder refuses every one\n  of them as \"no ladder\".\n- Those questions never reach the judge and are absent from the library.\n- new-2 lost 27 of 60 opened questions this way; new-3 lost 19 of 60.\n- Among the lost are matters the old system wins on:\n  - hyperscaler capex, M04, opened in both new draws;\n  - the Anthropic anchor investment, M17, in both;\n  - the Hugging Face acquisition, M19, in new-2;\n  - DRAM contract prices, M16, in both.\n- This class was identified on 2026-11-12 (D432). The Step 1 versions tried against it (c14, c15yc) did not pass their gates, so it was\n  never fixed.\n\nTogether the two mechanisms account for essentially all of b, the old-only matters (7–8): 5 company figures, M04 and M17, and M19 in\none draw.\n\n## Was the outcome predictable? Yes, and that is the process failure\n- The pass line is a lead: a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b. Under D382 the old system serves 5–6 figure matters the new one never can, so the new\n  system would need about 12 matters only it serves.\n- The matters its rules allow and the old one misses number about 12.\n- Even with the no-ladder loss fixed, the new system reaches about 7–8 against 10, which is no winner or a loss, never a lead.\n- **This could have been computed in minutes**, from the frozen list (7 figures flagged), D505, D432 and the D489 week, before any paid\n  send. AGENTS §7.2 asks for the upside of a step done perfectly to be measured before a phase targets it.\n- Neither the council (D665–D667) nor I computed it. Two days and about $145 measured a result that was knowable.\n- I added to the waste: a full Step 1 redo (about $21, 17 h) where a re-send of one item ($0.12) was enough.\n\n## The one thing to do next\n- **No new comparison run** until two things are settled at $0 or cents on stored data.\n- **(a) The Step 1 to ladder loss.** Questions must be cut to one figure, one period, one outcome; or the ladder splits a compound\n  question.\n  - Test: re-run the ladder on the 46 stored no-ladder cases with the fix, and count how many get a valid ladder and which key matters\n    they would cover.\n- **(b) Alex's decision on D382 for this comparison:**\n  - allow core-figure questions; or\n  - score the comparison on the 25 non-figure matters, where it stands now at 3 against 6 and could reach about 6 against 6 with (a).\n- **Before any run, compute the attainable verdict.**\n## 11. Do the kept financial figures reach the judgements of related questions? (D505) $0\n\n- **Alex:** \"进入相关问题的判断 (Recommended)\", the only option he chose: figures are evidence for related judgements, not a table and not\n  questions of their own; first a $0 check; \"有就报给你，没有就停\".\n- **Design** (`delivery/DELIVERY-CHECK-DESIGN.md`, version 2; council round 18 before any reader, four changes): the standard is PRD\n  10 §1 (\"the facts that can change its answer\", with onward reasoning), not a new one; a census by code of what each judgement\n  request was shown; both families list, one question a packet with a completion line, the table lines that bear on each of the\n  seven questions; each candidate read in the stored request and by a fresh pair shown everything the judge had; three outcomes\n  (finding, none, undecided).\n- **Result (D506; `delivery/DELIVERY-CHECK-RESULT.md`):** a judge is shown exactly the linked statements (196 links). One finding: the\n  credit-support question held \"nearly 2 gigawatts\" as a volume and never received the company's revenue opportunity per gigawatt\n  ($25 and $40 billion), kept from two articles (one linked to the Vera Rubin question only, one to none); all four readers say it\n  bears. Six open leads. No missing figure established for five questions. All seven judgements of that question were in its top\n  band; the effect of the figure was not measured.\n- **Council (mx round 19), consensus with corrections:** the finding stands as two figures, one question; a conditional indication\n  of scale, not a guarantee; no counterfactual, no rate; no census of the 389 unreceived statements (beyond his scope, blind to\n  statements linked elsewhere).\n- **Verdict:** reported to Alex as found; nothing built on one instance; an open defect of the new system.\n- **Lessons:** (1) delivery is read in the request, never inferred from a same-claim group; (2) a first reader's list is a lead,\n  what the judge already had decides (29 one-family candidates became five leads); (3) apply every condition of the frozen rule when\n  sorting by hand (one line was filed as delivered against the period rule); (4) write what was observed, not the counterfactual.\n\n## 12. How large is the gap? A census over everything the new system kept in the fresh week (D507) $0\n\n- **Alex:** \"先查清这类缺口有多大 (Recommended)\": all kept statements, those linked to another question included, against the seven questions;\n  the scope widened by his word beyond the financial figures; then decide whether to change anything.\n- **Design** (`delivery-class/CLASS-CENSUS-DESIGN.md`, version 2; council round 20 before any reader, three changes): the standard is\nbudget_replay.py\nbudget_step2.py\ncheck_budget.py\nrun_budgeted_draw.sh\nrg: hivemind/model.py: IO error for operation on hivemind/model.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n133:def ledger_lines(ledger_path):\n137:def attempt_ids(ledger_path):\n141:def ledger_stop(ledger_path):\n146:def ledger_total(ledger_path):\n157:def article_inputs(trace_path):\n181:def open_wal_store(path):\n213:def store_bytes(path):\n218:def free_bytes(folder):\n222:def held_by_another(error):\n227:def truncate_checkpoint(conn):\n238:def leave_wal(conn):\n441:def ladders_for(run, opened, days_of, cases_path=None, ladders_path=None):\n468:def ladder_configuration(archive_path=None):\n481:def calendar_days(first, last):\n488:def replay(run, output_folder, *, transport=None, cap_usd=0.66, sleep=None, limit=None, inputs=None, shared=None, end_day=None):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
