{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -l 'diagnostic-count|margin_rule|served by new' clean-arch docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review -g '*.py'\nrg --files | rg '(/model.py\"'$|matter.*'\"\\\\.json\"'$|comparison-2026-11-17/[''^/]+'\"\\\\.md\"'$)'\"' | head -50\np=poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\nls \\\"\"'$p/reading-diagnostic/deck\" | tail -30\nhead -c 2100 \"$p/reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-L1.json\"\ncat \"$p\"/run/new-3/judge/draw-new-3/adapter-counts.json\nhead -5 \"$p\"/run/new-2/judge/spend.jsonl'","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/model.py\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-grouping-repair-01/baseline/src/hivemind/model.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters-entries.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters-dedup-either-superseded.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/census/matters.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/matters-A2.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/calibration-matters.json\ndocs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/matters-A2.json\nC176.txt\nC177.txt\nC178.txt\nC179.txt\nC180.txt\nC181.txt\nC182.txt\nC183.txt\nC184.txt\nC185.txt\nC186.txt\nC187.txt\nC188.txt\nC189.txt\nC190.txt\nC191.txt\nC192.txt\nC193.txt\nC194.txt\nC195.txt\nC196.txt\nC197.txt\nC198.txt\nreadings.json\nround-0\nround-0.done\nround-1\nround-1.done\nround-2\nround-2.done\n[\n {\n  \"question_id\": \"Q1\",\n  \"question\": \"How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed under its AI-cloud model by the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\",\n  \"due\": \"2027-02-28\",\n  \"opened\": \"2026-07-01\",\n  \"opened_from\": \"nvblog:nvidia-unlocks-ai-compute-at-scale-capital-partners-to-power-ai-infrastructure-buildout\",\n  \"type\": \"figure\",\n  \"possible_answers\": [\n   \"Committed credit support is below $1 billion.\",\n   \"Committed credit support is at least $1 billion and below $5 billion.\",\n   \"Committed credit support is at least $5 billion and below $10 billion.\",\n   \"Committed credit support is at least $10 billion and below $20 billion.\",\n   \"Committed credit support is at least $20 billion.\"\n  ],\n  \"answer\": \"Committed credit support is at least $20 billion.\",\n  \"answer_index\": 4,\n  \"reasons\": \"The reference is NVIDIA’s disclosed $108.5 billion of AI-cloud guarantees and related agreements ($105 billion for SB Energy/PORTS-Pike plus $3.5 billion for other AI-cloud partners), which is rung 5. The implied amount is higher: NVIDIA said it would provide selective credit enhancement for nearly 2 GW for another frontier lab; scaling the $105 billion backstop for the reported 10 GW PORTS-Pike campus gives an indicative additional $21 billion, or roughly $129.5 billion total if additive. The estimate is uncertain and could overlap the $3.5 billion disclosure, but either way the outcome remains well above the $20 billion rung-5 boundary. The financing-platform pool and the $125 billion option are not themselves NVIDIA commitments; the reported pause concerns a separate partnership program and does not cancel the disclosed guarantees.\",\n  \"material\": [\n   {\n    \"tier\": \"rumour\",\n    \"speaker\": \"CommonWealth Magazine\",\n    \"original\": \"CommonWealth Magazine\",\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f71af3237fa3bee52a72c067\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"summary\": \"Nvidia is reportedly discussing a backstop of up to $250 billion for OpenAI's planned lease of a 10 GW data-center campus in Pike County, Ohio; the guarantee would cover lease and construction debt, not Nvidia chip{\n \"articles not completed by Step 1\": 0,\n \"ladder configuration\": \"clean-ladder-stage-a 14d0e269c8fe0335\",\n \"ladder answers file sha256\": \"c6a52a580a7ec30ed7b39788d6abc73669463544d6f809a0cd972b141e0b8d98\",\n \"views written from a ladder\": 41,\n \"quotes cut by the judge at 400 characters\": 1235,\n \"evidence written\": 5258,\n \"links from a laddered thesis to its view\": 2446,\n \"links written\": 2529,\n \"same_claims written\": 2934,\n \"judgements\": 1328,\n \"questions closed at their due day\": 1,\n \"records dropped: no verified passage\": 22,\n \"links lost with a dropped record\": 19,\n \"same_claims lost with a dropped record\": 22,\n \"revisions written\": 468,\n \"theses with no ladder\": 19,\n \"links to an unjudged thesis\": 1436,\n \"revisions lost with a dropped record\": 2,\n \"links to a closed question written (not judged)\": 1,\n \"store journal mode at the end\": \"delete\",\n \"judging usd this draw (charged: from tokens, or the reserve when no usage came back)\": 2.9951,\n \"judging usd of the whole limit so far (from its ledger)\": 2.9951\n}{\"attempt\": 1, \"reserve\": 0.0094866}\n{\"attempt\": 1, \"charge\": 0.0019753, \"known\": true}\n{\"attempt\": 2, \"reserve\": 0.0090019}\n{\"attempt\": 3, \"reserve\": 0.0097721}\n{\"attempt\": 2, \"charge\": 0.00077247, \"known\": true}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The stored runs show two different losses. Clean deliberately leaves standalone financial questions out, and its answer-choice step dropped questions about matters it was allowed to track, including hyperscaler spending. I’m checking which of those the old questions can recover in a replay."}}
