98, 104, 162, 232, 235, 254]), ('M15', 'Whether China formally permits imports of NVIDIA data center chips (H200) by 2027-01-31', '2026-09-09', [75, 77, 384]), ('M17', \"Whether NVIDIA commits an up-to-$10B anchor investment in Anthropic's IPO\", '2026-09-13', [189, 193, 195, 214, 233, 300, 310]), ('M18', 'NVIDIA FY2027 gross margin under memory-cost pressure (Q3 guide 74%, Q4 71-72%)', '2026-09-09', [75, 84, 196, 203]), ('M19', 'Whether NVIDIA closes the ~$12.9B Hugging Face acquisition (incl. regulatory clearance)', '2026-09-07', [3, 9, 20, 48, 56, 60, 95, 105, 146, 149, 187, 189, 214, 215, 224, 277, 398]), ('M31', 'NVIDIA AI cloud partner guarantee obligations at FY2027 year-end / NVIDIA total third-party guarantees and credit support for cloud/AI partners in the FY2027 10-K (vs up to $108.5B)', None, [51, 57, 61, 118, 126, 128, 254, 255, 320]), ('M32', 'NVIDIA neocloud capacity commitments at FY2027 year-end / NVIDIA cloud-service/neocloud capacity commitments, take-or-pay and revenue-floor backstops in the FY2027 10-K (vs $36B)', None, [126, 186, 187, 193, 247, 403])]\nnew-2 {'original': {'id': '1:E1', 'article': 1, 'input_id': 'nvblog:nvidia-unlocks-ai-compute-at-scale-capital-partners-to-power-ai-infrastructure-buildout', 'title': 'NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog', 'publisher': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'publication_date': '2026-07-01', 'summary': 'NVIDIA announced a new business model under which AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through a revenue-sharing and credit-support arrangement, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity.', 'passages': ['NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue‑sharing and credit‑support model.', 'This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity.'], 'verified_passages': [None, 'This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity.'], 'original_party': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'reporting_speaker': 'NVIDIA Corporation (corporate blog)', 'tier': 'party_statement', 'statement_date': '2026-07-01', 'statement_date_text': None, 'evidence_period': None, 'figures': [], 'thesis_ids': ['clean-1'], 'unresolved_thesis_ids': []}, 'members': [{'id': '8:e1', 'article': 8, 'input_id': 'gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45', 'title': \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers\nclean-5 2026-07-04 What will the big-four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures be over 2026 and 2027 — the aggregate demand pool underpinning NVIDIA's data-center revenue?\nclean-43 2026-08-28 Will NVIDIA complete its announced investment of up to US$10 billion in Anthropic, and how large will its equity stake in the AI lab become?\nreq ['model', 'messages', 'response_format', 'max_tokens'] {'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'ROLE\\n\\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading o\nraw ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'system_fingerprint', 'sent_request'] {'id': 'f5bc0498-d7ba-46c8-ba4f-f5fbff8a7a2e', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'created': 1794983777, 'model': 'deepseek-flash',\nres ['new_theses', 'evidence', 'unresolved_links', 'figure_issues', 'unfiled_evidence', 'unlinked_new_thesis_ids', 'new_thesis_ids'] {'new_theses': [{'local_id': 'T1', 'description': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have committed to AI cloud partners un\nreq ['model', 'messages', 'response_format', 'max_tokens'] {'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'ROLE\\n\\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading o\nraw ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'system_fingerprint', 'sent_request'] {'id': '2445ba88-3826-44c7-8934-d89187860301', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'created': 1794984432, 'model': 'deepseek-flash',\nres ['new_theses', 'evidence', 'unresolved_links', 'figure_issues', 'unfiled_evidence', 'unlinked_new_thesis_ids', 'new_thesis_ids'] {'new_theses': [], 'evidence': [{'local_id': 'e1', 'summary': \"NVIDIA recruited Nick Parker, a 26-year Microsoft veteran most\nnew-3 {'original': {'id': '1:E1', 'article': 1, 'input_id': 'nvblog:nvidia-unlocks-ai-compute-at-scale-capital-partners-to-power-ai-infrastructure-buildout', 'title': 'NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog', 'publisher': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'publication_date': '2026-07-01', 'summary': \"NVIDIA announced it is introducing a new business model in which AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers under a revenue-sharing and credit-support model: the AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services while NVIDIA earns both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity, which the company describes as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream. NVIDIA's lead statement frames the arrangement as partnering with AI clouds to deploy large-scale, multi-tenant AI factories with economics aligned through revenue sharing and credit support. No size, partner-level amount or signing date for the credit support is given.\", 'passages': ['NVIDIA is partnering with AI clouds to deploy large‑scale, multi‑tenant AI factories, aligning economics through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.', 'To address this, NVIDIA is introducing a new business model that opens up compute access to the fast‑growing AI ecosystem of startups, model builders, enterprises, research organizations and regional AI players.', 'This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of NVIDIA platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides NVIDIA with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.'], 'verified_passages': ['NVIDIA is partnering with\nclean-4 2026-07-04 Will the four largest AI hyperscalers' combined data center capital expenditures reach roughly $650 billion in calendar 2026, and Nvidia's projected $1 trillion in calendar 2027?\nclean-34 2026-08-19 How much will NVIDIA ultimately invest in Anthropic under the reported commitment of up to $10 billion, and what equity stake will it hold, as disclosed in its periodic filings?\nclean-58 2026-09-14 Will NVIDIA sign and fund its reported US$10 billion anchor investment in Anthropic's initial public offering, and will Anthropic complete that listing on its targeted pre-November-2026 timetable?\nreq ['model', 'messages', 'response_format', 'max_tokens'] {'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'ROLE\\n\\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading o\nraw ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'system_fingerprint', 'sent_request'] {'id': 'b1ceb88f-7aeb-484d-b5dc-05a3f281f941', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'created': 1794983777, 'model': 'deepseek-flash',\nres ['new_theses', 'evidence', 'unresolved_links', 'figure_issues', 'unfiled_evidence', 'unlinked_new_thesis_ids', 'new_thesis_ids'] {'new_theses': [{'local_id': 'T1', 'description': 'How much credit support will NVIDIA have extended to AI cloud partners und\nreq ['model', 'messages', 'response_format', 'max_tokens'] {'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'ROLE\\n\\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading o\nraw ['id', 'object', 'created', 'model', 'choices', 'usage', 'system_fingerprint', 'sent_request'] {'id': 'e23a1c74-6f05-48fe-8076-63b1c5de8fee', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'created': 1794984346, 'model': 'deepseek-flash',\nres ['new_theses', 'evidence', 'unresolved_links', 'figure_issues', 'unfiled_evidence', 'unlinked_new_thesis_ids', 'new_thesis_ids'] {'new_theses': [], 'evidence': [{'local_id': 'ev-1', 'summary': \"NVIDIA appointed Nick Parker, a 26-year Microsoft veteran wh\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\\\")\nr=json.loads((p/\\\"reading-diagnostic/deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())\nfor f in sorted((p/\\\"reading-diagnostic/mapping-out\\\").glob(\\\"library-*.json\\\")):\n print(f.name)\n v=json.loads(f.read_text())\n for q in v:\n  s=q[\\\"question\\\"].lower()\n  if (\\\"four\\\" in s and \\\"capit\\\" in s and \\\"2026\\\" in s) or (\\\"anthropic\\\" in s and (\\\"ipo\\\" in s or \\\"anchor\\\" in s)):\n   print(q[\\\"question_id\\\"],q[\\\"opened\\\"],q[\\\"due\\\"],q[\\\"question\\\"],q[\\\"answer\\\"],q[\\\"reasons\\\"][:350])\nfor d in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n l=json.loads((p/f\\\"run/{d}/step2/library.json\\\").read_text())\n found={\\\"capex\\\":[],\\\"anthropic\\\":[]}\n for g in l[\\\"groups\\\"].values():\n  for e in [g[\\\"original\\\"],*g[\\\"members\\\"]]:\n   s=e[\\\"summary\\\"].lower()\n   if not any(e[\\\"verified_passages\\\"]): continue\n   if \\\"2026\\\" in s and any(x in s for x in (\\\"hyperscaler\\\",\\\"amazon\\\",\\\"meta\\\")) and (\\\"700\\\" in s or \\\"725\\\" in s or \\\"750\\\" in s or \\\"660\\\" in s or \\\"650\\\" in s):\n    found[\\\"capex\\\"].append(e)\n   if \\\"anthropic\\\" in s and \\\"ipo\\\" in s and (\\\"anchor\\\" in s or \\\"invest\\\" in s):\n    found[\\\"anthropic\\\"].append(e)\n print(d)\n for k,es in found.items():\n  print(k,len(es))\n  for e in es[-6:]:\n   print(e[\\\"publication_date\\\"],e[\\\"id\\\"],e[\\\"thesis_ids\\\"],e[\\\"input_id\\\"],e[\\\"summary\\\"][:380])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\\\")\nr=json.loads((p/\\\"reading-diagnostic/deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())\nfor f in sorted((p/\\\"reading-diagnostic/mapping-out\\\").glob(\\\"library-*.json\\\")):\n print(f.name)\n v=json.loads(f.read_text())\n for q in v:\n  s=q[\\\"question\\\"].lower()\n  if (\\\"four\\\" in s and \\\"capit\\\" in s and \\\"2026\\\" in s) or (\\\"anthropic\\\" in s and (\\\"ipo\\\" in s or \\\"anchor\\\" in s)):\n   print(q[\\\"question_id\\\"],q[\\\"opened\\\"],q[\\\"due\\\"],q[\\\"question\\\"],q[\\\"answer\\\"],q[\\\"reasons\\\"][:350])\nfor d in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n l=json.loads((p/f\\\"run/{d}/step2/library.json\\\").read_text())\n found={\\\"capex\\\":[],\\\"anthropic\\\":[]}\n for g in l[\\\"groups\\\"].values():\n  for e in [g[\\\"original\\\"],*g[\\\"members\\\"]]:\n   s=e[\\\"summary\\\"].lower()\n   if not any(e[\\\"verified_passages\\\"]): continue\n   if \\\"2026\\\" in s and any(x in s for x in (\\\"hyperscaler\\\",\\\"amazon\\\",\\\"meta\\\")) and (\\\"700\\\" in s or \\\"725\\\" in s or \\\"750\\\" in s or \\\"660\\\" in s or \\\"650\\\" in s):\n    found[\\\"capex\\\"].append(e)\n   if \\\"anthropic\\\" in s and \\\"ipo\\\" in s and (\\\"anchor\\\" in s or \\\"invest\\\" in s):\n    found[\\\"anthropic\\\"].append(e)\n print(d)\n for k,es in found.items():\n  print(k,len(es))\n  for e in es[-6:]:\n   print(e[\\\"publication_date\\\"],e[\\\"id\\\"],e[\\\"thesis_ids\\\"],e[\\\"input_id\\\"],e[\\\"summary\\\"][:380])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"library-L1.json\nQ5 2026-07-04 2027-03-31 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion. The market reference is roughly $720–$745 billion for the four companies, which is rung 4. A direct four-hyperscaler estimate of $760 billion and tracking near $745 billion support an implied outcome around $750–$760 billion. Newer estimates of nearly $800 billion refer to the top five, not these four, so the fifth company cannot be counted in full\nQ40 2026-09-14 2026-09-20 Will NVIDIA invest $10 billion to anchor Anthropic's IPO by 2026-09-20? NVIDIA does not complete an investment of $10 billion to anchor Anthropic's IPO by 2026-09-20. The reference is rung 2: no market consensus or company guidance is supplied, and the reported expectation that Anthropic's IPO would be completed before the November midterms does not put NVIDIA's investment by September 20. Reuters-linked reports that NVIDIA is considering up to $10 billion and that Anthropic is discussing an anchor role push tow\nlibrary-L2.json\nQ6 2026-07-04 2027-02-28 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $800 billion. The market reference is roughly $720–$745 billion for the four hyperscalers, which sits in rung 4 (e5014). The evidence still implies about $750 billion: the four-company tracking estimate near $745 billion and the separate top-four estimate of $760 billion bracket that level; company capex revisions and recent cloud-demand indicators support the u\nQ47 2026-09-14 2026-09-20 Will NVIDIA agree to anchor Anthropic’s IPO with an investment of $10 billion by September 20, 2026? NVIDIA has not agreed by September 20, 2026, to anchor Anthropic’s IPO with a $10 billion investment. The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus, company guidance, or NVIDIA commitment is supplied. The reports of advanced talks and consideration of an investment of up to $10 billion this week raise the chance of Yes, but they do not report agreement to anchor the IPO for $10 billion. Given the short time to the deadline and the gap between c\nQ48 2026-09-14 2027-03-14 Will NVIDIA agree to invest US$10 billion in Anthropic’s planned IPO by March 14, 2027? NVIDIA agrees to invest US$10 billion in Anthropic’s IPO by March 14, 2027. The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus, company guidance, or stated plan says an agreement has been reached, so the status quo is no agreement by the deadline. The specific reports of negotiations and NVIDIA weighing an investment of up to US$10 billion make an agreement by March 14, 2027 more likely than no agreement, despite the amount\nlibrary-L3.json\nlibrary-L5.json\nlibrary-L6.json\nQ6 2026-07-04 2027-02-28 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion. The market reference for the four companies is roughly $720–745 billion, which sits in rung 4. The evidence implies about $760 billion for the four: the direct four-company estimate is $760 billion, and the later Amazon and Alphabet figures are consistent with company spending plans already reflected in that estimate, so they should not be added ag\nQ45 2026-09-14 2027-09-14 Will NVIDIA complete an investment in Anthropic’s potential IPO by September 14, 2027? NVIDIA completes an investment in Anthropic by September 14, 2027. The reference is rung 2 (No): absent a market consensus or stated completion schedule, the default is that NVIDIA has not completed an investment by September 14, 2027. The specific Reuters-attributed reports that NVIDIA is discussing or weighing an anchor investment of up to $10 billion, together with the report that Anthropic selected Nasdaq for \nQ46 2026-09-14 2026-09-20 Will NVIDIA agree to invest $10 billion in Anthropic’s IPO by September 20, 2026? NVIDIA agrees to invest $10 billion in Anthropic’s IPO by September 20, 2026. The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or announced NVIDIA plan is supplied. The reported advanced talks and consideration of an investment of up to $10 billion, tied to anchoring the IPO and a reported timing during the week of September 14, make agreement by September 20 the more likely outcome. The reports still describe a ceiling rat\nnew-2\ncapex 11\n2026-07-26 536:e2 ['clean-5'] gnews:fddb23b609fb42502a9aabce The four large AI hyperscalers — Alphabet, Amazon, Microsoft and Meta Platforms — said earlier in 2026 that they plan to spend about $650 billion on capital expenditures this year (2026), according to the article.\n2026-08-01 697:e2 ['clean-5'] gnews:c3795c657a584ee726778e8f NVIDIA projects that AI hyperscalers will spend $1 trillion or more on data-center capital expenditure in 2027, up from an estimated $650 billion in 2026, according to the article.\n2026-08-13 842:ev-1 ['clean-5'] gnews:282e6723858d56e9cb5b100e NVIDIA has told investors it expects $1 trillion of AI hyperscaler capital expenditures in 2027 (\"next year\" relative to the item's 2026-08-13 publication), compared with 2026 projections of about $650 billion as of the start of that year, per the article's restatement of NVIDIA's guidance.\n2026-07-26 536:e5 ['clean-5'] gnews:fddb23b609fb42502a9aabce The article's author estimates total AI capital-expenditure spending this year (2026) at $875 billion, obtained by adding spending from OpenAI, Anthropic and international governments to the four hyperscalers' roughly $650 billion.\n2026-08-18 917:ev-1 ['clean-5'] gnews:d6efd802b62a436ca6e8f9be An unnamed estimate cited in the article puts combined 2026 capital expenditures for Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet and Meta Platforms at around $700 billion, with roughly two-thirds of that directed toward AI infrastructure rather than traditional cloud; the article separately says the hyperscalers themselves say they plan to spend hundreds of billions of dollars in 2026 alone, a\n2026-08-24 1020:ev-10 ['clean-5'] gnews:d6f3abdac8b80c3c4256fc18 tastylive reports a projection that the four largest hyperscalers — Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon and Meta — will spend a combined $700 billion or more on capital expenditures in 2026.\nanthropic 9\n2026-09-15 1694:ev-1 ['clean-43'] gnews:a1af1bb8840fa4ec9e52bcb0 On 2026-09-13 Reuters reported that Anthropic is in talks to bring NVIDIA in as an anchor investor in an IPO that could raise as much as $100 billion at a valuation of around $2 trillion, and that NVIDIA is reportedly considering an investment of up to $10 billion; no terms are confirmed and the talks are attributed to unnamed sources.\n2026-09-15 1706:e1 ['clean-43'] gnews:06b55f52d782a58df06d9f4f NVIDIA is reported to be in advanced talks, according to unnamed people familiar with the discussions, to invest up to US$10 billion in Anthropic's planned IPO.\n2026-09-17 1781:ev-1 ['clean-43'] gnews:df74df86a5a6cfd06fe7cbb3 Reuters reported, per barchart.com, that Anthropic is discussing bringing Nvidia in as an anchor investor for its planned IPO, and that Nvidia is reportedly considering an investment of up to $10 billion; neither company has confirmed the discussions.\n2026-09-14 1664:e6 ['clean-43', 'clean-44'] gnews:4dca50e22bd9f158d2a04186 Anthropic's annualised revenue run rate rose from approximately $9 billion at the end of 2025 to more than $65 billion by mid-2026, per fxleaders.com, which cites this in describing NVIDIA's computing partnership with the AI lab and its prospective IPO investment.\n2026-09-14 1668:ev-2 ['clean-26'] gnews:65814ac898f65c6b360be321 Anthropic's annualized revenue run rate eclipsed US$65 billion by late July 2026, up from approximately US$9 billion at the end of 2025, according to investingnews.com's report on the company's IPO push.\n2026-09-14 1668:ev-3 ['clean-26'] gnews:65814ac898f65c6b360be321 Anthropic is projecting US$190 billion to US$200 billion in revenue by 2028 to support a roughly US$2 trillion IPO valuation, following a US$65 billion private funding round in May 2026 that valued it at US$965 billion post-money, per investingnews.com.\nnew-3\ncapex 15\n2026-08-13 841:ev-1 ['clean-4'] gnews:4136a4be5d63d394bd302f15 Wall Street consensus expects five hyperscalers — Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, Microsoft and Oracle — to spend about $733 billion in 2026, up sharply from earlier forecasts. The figure covers five companies including Oracle, and is above the roughly $650 billion 2026 plan for the big four tracked in the open thesis.\n2026-08-18 917:e1 ['clean-4'] gnews:d6efd802b62a436ca6e8f9be Fool.com contributor Micah Zimmerman, citing an unnamed estimate, put combined calendar-2026 capital expenditure for Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet and Meta Platforms at around $700 billion, roughly two-thirds of it directed to AI infrastructure rather than traditional cloud; he also wrote that the hyperscalers themselves say they plan to spend hundreds of billions of dollars in 2\n2026-08-24 1020:ev-6 ['clean-4'] gnews:d6f3abdac8b80c3c4256fc18 tastylive's preview projects that the four largest hyperscalers — Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon and Meta — will spend a combined $700 billion or more on capital expenditures in 2026.\n2026-09-16 1751:ev-1 ['clean-4'] gnews:b98d0a9596b1d1e0a9609645 MarketBeat, in its 2026-09-16 article, reports that capital expenditure plans among the leading AI hyperscalers total over $700 billion, citing the figure as evidence of the scale of AI infrastructure spending; the item does not state which quarters or years the plans cover.\n2026-08-19 944:ev-4 ['clean-4'] gnews:7ad5bd51d8d392d6f45c966f The article estimates that the four largest hyperscalers — Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta Platforms — are expected to spend roughly $700 billion on AI chips this year (calendar 2026), and that the figure is likely to rise next year. The estimate is the author's, and the measure is AI-chip spending rather than total data-centre capex.\n2026-08-24 1030:ev-1 ['clean-4'] gnews:ef33a7818940138595f3e2ef In a 2026-08-24 column, The Motley Fool reported that the five hyperscalers — Microsoft, Amazon, Alphabet, Meta Platforms and Oracle — all either reaffirmed or boosted their capital expenditure plans for the year, pushing their combined planned outlay north of $700 billion.\nanthropic 6\n2026-07-17 330:e1 [] gnews:5bb8520ec549575a4080c93c OpenAI and rival Anthropic, which Euronews describes as two of the most valuable private companies in history, have filed to go public (IPO); the article frames their planned listings as intensifying investor questions about whether the large investments being made in AI will pay off.\n2026-09-14 1664:e6 [] gnews:4dca50e22bd9f158d2a04186 Anthropic's annualised revenue run rate rose from approximately $9 billion at the end of 2025 to over $65 billion by mid-2026, per the article, which frames NVIDIA's potential IPO anchor investment as an extension of their computing partnership.\n2026-09-14 1664:e5 ['clean-34'] gnews:4dca50e22bd9f158d2a04186 NVIDIA is reportedly considering anchoring Anthropic's initial public offering with a $10 billion investment, according to Reuters; the offering could sell up to $100 billion of shares at a valuation around $2 trillion, which would make it potentially the largest IPO in history.\n2026-09-14 1668:ev-1 ['clean-34', 'clean-58'] gnews:65814ac898f65c6b360be321 Anthropic is negotiating to secure NVIDIA as an anchor investor for an IPO it aims to launch before the US midterm elections in November 2026, raising up to US$100 billion and valuing Anthropic at roughly US$2 trillion; according to a Reuters exclusive, NVIDIA is weighing a US$10 billion commitment to the offering. No signed terms, price or closing date are given.\n2026-09-15 1694:e1 ['clean-34', 'clean-58'] gnews:a1af1bb8840fa4ec9e52bcb0 On 13 September 2026 Reuters reported that Anthropic is in talks to bring NVIDIA in as an anchor investor in an IPO that could raise as much as $100 billion at a valuation of around $2 trillion, and that Nvidia is reportedly considering an investment of up to $10 billion. The talks are reported, not agreed; no terms or signing date are given.\n2026-09-17 1781:e2 ['clean-34', 'clean-58'] gnews:df74df86a5a6cfd06fe7cbb3 NVIDIA is reportedly in discussions to become an anchor investor in Anthropic's planned IPO, considering an investment of up to $10 billion, according to Reuters; neither company has confirmed the discussions, and the article says the investment amount and final terms may differ from early reports.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17\\\")\ndef db(path): \n c=sqlite3.connect(\\\"file:\\\"+str(path)+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n return c\ns=0\nfor d,lib,ids in ((\\\"old-2\\\",\\\"L1\\\",[\\\"Q5\\\",\\\"Q40\\\"]),(\\\"old-3\\\",\\\"L2\\\",[\\\"Q6\\\",\\\"Q47\\\"])):\n lib={x[\\\"question_id\\\"]:x for x in json.loads((p/f\\\"reading-diagnostic/mapping-out/library-{lib}.json\\\").read_text())}\n views=db(p/f\\\"run/{d}/prod/views.sqlite\\\");a=db(p/f\\\"run/{d}/prod/archive.sqlite\\\")\n for q in ids:\n  v=views.execute(\\\"select * from views where question=?\\\",(lib[q][\\\"question\\\"],)).fetchone()\n  j=views.execute(\\\"select * from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc limit 1\\\",(v[\\\"view_id\\\"],)).fetchone()\n  z=a.execute(\\\"select purpose,model,response_json,request_json from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(j[\\\"call_id\\\"],)).fetchone()\n  r=json.loads(z[\\\"response_json\\\"])[\\\"usage\\\"]\n  n,o=r[\\\"prompt_tokens\\\"],r[\\\"completion_tokens\\\"]; c=(r.get(\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\") or {}).get(\\\"cached_tokens\\\",0)\n  usd=(.10*(n-c)+.01*c+.50*o)/1e6;s+=usd\n  print(d,q,v[\\\"view_id\\\"],v[\\\"created_from_input\\\"],j[\\\"publication_day\\\"],j[\\\"seq\\\"],z[\\\"model\\\"],n,o,c,usd)\nprint(\\\"four cost\\\",s,\\\"eight est\\\",s*2)\nfor d in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n l=json.loads((p/f\\\"run/{d}/step2/library.json\\\").read_text())\n print(d)\n for g in l[\\\"groups\\\"].values():\n  for e in [g[\\\"original\\\"],*g[\\\"members\\\"]]:\n   t=e[\\\"summary\\\"].lower()\n   if any(e[\\\"verified_passages\\\"]) and ((\\\"745 billion\\\" in t or \\\"760 billion\\\" in t) and (\\\"capex\\\" in t or \\\"capital exp\\\" in t) or (\\\"billion per gigawatt\\\" in t and (\\\"40 billion\\\" in t or \\\"25 billion\\\" in t))):\n    print(e[\\\"id\\\"],e[\\\"publication_date\\\"],e[\\\"input_id\\\"],e[\\\"thesis_ids\\\"],e[\\\"summary\\\"][:320])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
