{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\nfor draw in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n db=sqlite3.connect(f\\\"file:{root/draw}/step1/trace.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n for k in (982,1423,1680,1694,1751):\n  _,i,b,req,raw,res,a,status,err,usd,retry=db.execute(\\\"select * from trace where sequence=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone()\n  raw=json.loads(raw)\n  answer=json.loads(raw[\\\"choices\\\"][0][\\\"message\\\"][\\\"content\\\"])\n  res=json.loads(res)\n  print(draw,k,status)\n  for row in answer.get(\\\"evidence\\\",[]):\n   s=row.get(\\\"summary\\\",\\\"\\\")\n   sl=s.lower()\n   if (\\\"hyperscaler\\\" in sl and (\\\"760\\\" in sl or \\\"745\\\" in sl or \\\"700\\\" in sl)) or (\\\"anchor\\\" in sl and \\\"anthropic\\\" in sl) or (\\\"gigawatt\\\" in sl and \\\"rubin\\\" in sl):\n    print(\\\"raw:\\\", s[:310])\n  for row in res[\\\"evidence\\\"]:\n   s=row.get(\\\"summary\\\",\\\"\\\")\n   sl=s.lower()\n   if (\\\"hyperscaler\\\" in sl and (\\\"760\\\" in sl or \\\"745\\\" in sl or \\\"700\\\" in sl)) or (\\\"anchor\\\" in sl and \\\"anthropic\\\" in sl) or (\\\"gigawatt\\\" in sl and \\\"rubin\\\" in sl):\n    print(\\\"saved:\\\",row.get(\\\"links\\\"),row.get(\\\"local_id\\\"))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\nfor draw in (\\\"new-2\\\",\\\"new-3\\\"):\n db=sqlite3.connect(f\\\"file:{root/draw}/step1/trace.sqlite?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\n for k in (982,1423,1680,1694,1751):\n  _,i,b,req,raw,res,a,status,err,usd,retry=db.execute(\\\"select * from trace where sequence=?\\\",(k,)).fetchone()\n  raw=json.loads(raw)\n  answer=json.loads(raw[\\\"choices\\\"][0][\\\"message\\\"][\\\"content\\\"])\n  res=json.loads(res)\n  print(draw,k,status)\n  for row in answer.get(\\\"evidence\\\",[]):\n   s=row.get(\\\"summary\\\",\\\"\\\")\n   sl=s.lower()\n   if (\\\"hyperscaler\\\" in sl and (\\\"760\\\" in sl or \\\"745\\\" in sl or \\\"700\\\" in sl)) or (\\\"anchor\\\" in sl and \\\"anthropic\\\" in sl) or (\\\"gigawatt\\\" in sl and \\\"rubin\\\" in sl):\n    print(\\\"raw:\\\", s[:310])\n  for row in res[\\\"evidence\\\"]:\n   s=row.get(\\\"summary\\\",\\\"\\\")\n   sl=s.lower()\n   if (\\\"hyperscaler\\\" in sl and (\\\"760\\\" in sl or \\\"745\\\" in sl or \\\"700\\\" in sl)) or (\\\"anchor\\\" in sl and \\\"anthropic\\\" in sl) or (\\\"gigawatt\\\" in sl and \\\"rubin\\\" in sl):\n    print(\\\"saved:\\\",row.get(\\\"links\\\"),row.get(\\\"local_id\\\"))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"new-2 982 complete\nraw: The top four hyperscalers plan $760 billion of capital expenditure in 2026 alone, according to Fool.com — the aggregate hyperscaler capex pool that underpins data-center accelerator demand.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-5', 'relevance': \"Directly supplies a 2026 figure for the big-four hyperscalers' combined data-center capex pool that clean-5 tracks, indicating the size of the demand pool behind NVIDIA's data-center revenue.\"}] ev-5\nnew-2 1423 complete\nraw: CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA can reach $40 billion of revenue per gigawatt of AI computing capacity with Vera Rubin, versus about $25 billion per gigawatt with Blackwell and about $18 billion per gigawatt with Hopper, as NVIDIA sells more of the complete rack (accelerators, networking and its own processors)\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-5', 'relevance': \"The per-gigawatt revenue figures quantify how much NVIDIA revenue each gigawatt of installed AI capacity generates (rising from ~$18B Hopper to ~$40B Vera Rubin), refining how the hyperscalers' capex pool tracked by the thesis translates into NVIDIA data-center revenue; the $40B is a company expectation, not a realized figure.\"}] e4\nnew-2 1680 complete\nraw: The article states that the four top hyperscalers — Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta Platforms — are expected to spend roughly $720 billion to $745 billion on capital expenditures in 2026, with a large portion directed toward AI infrastructure.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-5', 'relevance': 'Gives an expected 2026 combined capex figure for the four named hyperscalers, the aggregate demand pool the thesis tracks; note the figure is total capex, not data-center capex alone, and is an expectation rather than a reported actual.'}] ev4\nnew-2 1694 complete\nraw: On 2026-09-13 Reuters reported that Anthropic is in talks to bring NVIDIA in as an anchor investor in an IPO that could raise as much as $100 billion at a valuation of around $2 trillion, and that NVIDIA is reportedly considering an investment of up to $10 billion; no terms are confirmed and the talks are att\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-43', 'relevance': \"Reported talks about NVIDIA taking up to $10 billion of an Anthropic IPO stake bear directly on whether NVIDIA's announced up-to-$10B Anthropic investment is signed/completed and on the size of its stake; unconfirmed, so it does not establish the investment.\"}] ev-1\nnew-2 1751 complete\nraw: MarketBeat stated that capital expenditure plans among the leading hyperscalers total over $700 billion, which it cited as underscoring the AI infrastructure spend; no period, company split or sourcing is given.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-5', 'relevance': 'The aggregate of hyperscaler capex plans at over $700 billion bears directly on the size of the big-four data-center capex pool the thesis tracks, but the item gives no period and no company-level split, so it informs rather than answers the question.'}] e4\nnew-3 982 complete\nraw: The four largest AI hyperscalers plan $760 billion of capital expenditure in calendar 2026, according to the Motley Fool analyst, who cites the figure as the basis for investor worry about how long the AI build-out can keep growing.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-4', 'relevance': 'A stated 2026 combined capex plan for the four largest hyperscalers is the same aggregate clean-4 tracks (~$650 billion for calendar 2026); at $760 billion it is a higher figure for the same spending pool that drives Nvidia data-center demand.'}] e5\nnew-3 1423 complete\nraw: NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress, as reported, quantified the company's revenue per gigawatt of installed computing capacity: about $18 billion per gigawatt with Hopper, rising to $25 billion with Blackwell, and reaching $40 billion per gigawatt with Vera Rubin — the increase coming from selling more of the AI rack (\nsaved: [] e4\nnew-3 1680 complete\nraw: Zacks reports that the four top hyperscalers — Amazon, Alphabet, Microsoft and Meta Platforms — are expected to spend roughly $720 billion to $745 billion on capital expenditures in 2026, with a large portion directed toward AI infrastructure.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-4', 'relevance': 'The expected $720-$745 billion combined 2026 hyperscaler capex is above the roughly $650 billion level tracked by the thesis, directly informing the capex question.'}] e4\nnew-3 1694 complete\nraw: On 13 September 2026 Reuters reported that Anthropic is in talks to bring NVIDIA in as an anchor investor in an IPO that could raise as much as $100 billion at a valuation of around $2 trillion, and that Nvidia is reportedly considering an investment of up to $10 billion. The talks are reported, not agreed; n\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-58', 'relevance': \"Directly the reported anchor investment of up to $10 billion in Anthropic's IPO and the listing the thesis tracks; the talks are unconfirmed and unsigned, so they are evidence of a possible commitment, not a signed one.\"}, {'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-34', 'relevance': \"Bears on the eventual size and terms of Nvidia's reported up-to-$10 billion investment in Anthropic, here framed as an IPO-stage anchorship at a roughly $2 trillion implied valuation.\"}] e1\nnew-3 1751 complete\nraw: MarketBeat, in its 2026-09-16 article, reports that capital expenditure plans among the leading AI hyperscalers total over $700 billion, citing the figure as evidence of the scale of AI infrastructure spending; the item does not state which quarters or years the plans cover.\nsaved: [{'target_type': 'existing', 'target_id': 'clean-4', 'relevance': \"Supplies an aggregate figure (over $700 billion) for leading hyperscalers' capex plans that bears on the thesis's question about their combined data-centre capex (~$650bn calendar 2026, $1 trillion 2027). The item gives no period for the $700bn, so it cannot be read as either the 2026 or the 2027 figure.\"}] ev-1\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
