{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"**Use the old system to open questions, the clean system to read and organize evidence, and the same judge to answer them.** Both clean runs kept a $760 billion estimate for four hyperscalers’ 2026 spending. Both attached it to a question that also asked about 2027. The answer-choice step refused the combined question, and later articles kept filing evidence under it. [Refusal review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/PATH-TO-PASS.md)\n\n**What I checked.** The old system served 10 of 32 matters. Clean served 2–3, with no repeatable win of its own. Clean kept 211–214 of 234 helpful facts versus 162–171 in the older, separate extraction runs. Its search found 141 of 143 known earlier versions, with one clear wrong merge in 57 comparisons. Its answer-choice step declined 27 and 19 of 60 questions. [Stored readings](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/diagnostic-count.json) · [Clean PRD](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md#L79)\n\n**Proposed merge**\n\n- **Opening and choices.** Use v118’s proposals, matcher and duplicate-question check. Give each accepted question one ID and one outcome before the next article sees it. Reuse old numeric cutoffs when they pass clean’s range, reference and direction checks. Use clean’s explicit pending outcome for events. A refused proposal stays out of the open list.\n- **Reading and judging.** Give c8 the accepted questions and the article. Use clean Steps 2–3 to find repeats across the company, preserve each source and its wording, and link revisions to earlier statements. Keep useful unlinked evidence for later filing under D383. Feed relevant evidence through the existing adapter to the frozen daily judge and closing step. Under D382/D505, NVIDIA’s own figures inform related questions. Standalone figure questions would require Alex’s exception. [Decisions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md#L726)\n\n**Smallest test.** Score September 7–20, with stored history from July 1. Pair old-2/new-2 and old-3/new-3 for four-hyperscaler spending and Anthropic’s IPO investment. Hold the old questions and choices fixed. Trace verified clean evidence into each proposed judge input. **Pass** if both matters receive the decisive evidence in both pairs, with zero links to refused questions. Reject five-company or 2027 totals as direct answers, keep reported talks distinct from a signed commitment, and verify that an unrelated NVIDIA figure opens no question.\n\n**Attainable result and cost.** Both clean draws contain the needed passages, so 4/4 handoffs are attainable at $0. The four corresponding archived judge calls cost 0.685¢ from stored token usage. The test checks the handoff. Automatic opening, fresh answers and release readiness remain unmeasured. Across all 32 matters, combining already-supported results ceilings at **6** under D382/D505, or **10** with Alex’s exception. A release lead still needs respectively **9** or **5** new-only wins. [Stored runs and ledgers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run) · [Release decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md#L1020)\n\n**Main risk.** A question can survive while its meaning shifts. Total capital spending and data-center spending already appear side by side in the stored material. Matching the companies and year alone could make the judge confidently answer the wrong question."}}
